+When ranking insertion candidates, the raw benefit-to-cost score is multiplied by 1.06 if another selected project has the same group label. This is a heuristic ordering bonus only. The implementation defines no prerequisite, mutual-exclusion, group-completion, or joint-benefit term, and the bonus does not enter the four objectives, the budget constraint, or environmental selection. \texttt{Ablation-NoDependencyMoves} disables the multiplier; \texttt{Ablation-LowDependencyDensity} changes group labels as a separate stress variant. Neither comparison operationalizes or demonstrates a dependency benefit.
 
 \subsection{Feasibility Recovery}\label{feasibility-recovery}
 
-Every initial or offspring portfolio that violates the budget is repaired deterministically. The selected project with the lowest benefit-to-cost ratio is removed until the portfolio is affordable. Because each step removes one selected project and the empty portfolio is feasible, repair terminates after at most \(\|x\|_0\) drops. Each restoration step is recorded as a repair event.
